arch</source><year>2005</year><volume>6</volume><fpage>22</fpage><lpage>29</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B41"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Ari&#x000f1;o-Biasco</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Tadd</surname><given-names>W</given-names></name><name><surname>Boix-Ferer</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Dignity and older people: The voice of professionals</article-title><source>Quality in Ageing &#x02013; Policy, practice and research</source><year>2005</year><volume>6</volume><fpage>30</fpage><lpage>36</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B42"><citation citation-type="other"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Lee</surname><given-names>TFD</given-names></name><name><surname>Low</surname><given-names>PLL</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Provision of culturally sensitive residential care-respecting privacy and dignity in a Chinese context</article-title><source>Proceedings of 18th Congress of the International Association of Gerontology</source><year>2005</year><fpage>77</fpage></citation></ref><ref id="B43"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Haddock</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Towards further clarification of the concept 'dignity'</article-title><source>Journal of Advanced Nursing</source><year>1996</year><volume>24</volume><fpage>924</fpage><lpage>931</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8933251</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1111/j.1365-2648.1996.tb02927.x</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B44"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Gallagher</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Dignity and Respect for Dignity &#x02013; Two Key Health Professional Values: Implications for Nursing Practice</article-title><source>Nursing Ethics</source><year>2004</year><volume>11</volume><fpage>587</fpage><lpage>599</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15597939</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1191/0969733004ne744oa</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B45"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><collab>Health Advisory Service 2000</collab></person-group><source>Not because they are old' An independent inquiry into the care of older people</source><year>1999</year><publisher-name>London, Help the Aged</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B46"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Robb</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name></person-group><source>Sans Everything: A Case to Answer</source><year>1967</year><publisher-name>London, Nelson</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B47"><citation citation-type="other"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Street-Porter</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Now I know Pat didn't die in vain</article-title><source>The Independent newspaper 26th November, 2006</source><ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://tinyurl.com/3x9pbr"/><comment>Accessed 07/02/08</comment></citation></ref><ref id="B48"><citation citation-type="other"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Darzi</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Health: Mixed-sex Wards</article-title><source>Lords Hansard 28th January 2008</source><ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://tinyurl.com/2xpau8"/><comment>Accessed 07/02/08</comment></citation></ref><ref id="B49"><citation citation-type="other"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Carvel</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><source>Johnson pledges to end mixed-sex accommodation in NHS The Guardian newspaper May 1st 2008</source><ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.guardian.co.uk/politics/2008/may/01/alanjohnson.nhs"/><comment>accessed 06/06/08</comment></citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>